# Names and purpose only. Inject real values through the deployment secret store.
# APP_ENV — local, test, preview, staging or production; explicit for build/start.
# APP_URL — canonical application origin, HTTPS for deployed environments.
# VERCEL_ENV — supplied by Vercel; must agree with APP_ENV.
# SUPABASE_URL — environment-specific hosted Supabase origin.
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY — environment-specific public API key, kept server-side here.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY — privileged server-only key; never expose to a client.
# SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF — identifier matching the Supabase origin.
# SUPABASE_ENVIRONMENT — data environment; must equal APP_ENV.
# PRODUCTION_SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF — production reference guard for project isolation.
# RATE_LIMIT_KEY_SECRET — at least 32 characters, for pseudonymous quota identities.
# RESEND_API_KEY — server-only email provider credential.
# EMAIL_FROM — verified sending identity.
# EMAIL_SANDBOX_RECIPIENT — mandatory recipient override for non-production email.
# TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY — bot challenge site identifier.
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY — server-only bot challenge verification credential.
# SENTRY_DSN — environment-specific error ingestion endpoint.
# PDF_WORKER_URL — authenticated PDF worker service endpoint.
# PDF_WORKER_TOKEN — server-only PDF worker authentication credential.
# QUEUE_SIGNING_KEY — server-only callback/job signature credential.
# PAYMENT_PROVIDER — disabled, stripe or paddle; provider onboarding is a launch decision.
# PAYMENT_API_KEY — server-only payment provider credential.
# PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET — server-only webhook verification credential.
# INDEXNOW_KEY — proof of ownership for search submission.
# ANALYTICS_SITE_ID — environment-specific consent-aware analytics identifier.
# ENABLE_PAYMENTS — true only for an approved, configured provider.
# ENABLE_REGULATED_DOCUMENTS — true only with recorded regulatory approval.
# ENABLE_TRANSACTIONAL_EMAIL — true only with approved, configured delivery.
# PAYMENTS_APPROVED — recorded payment, merchant and webhook readiness approval.
# REGULATED_DOCUMENTS_APPROVED — recorded legal/regulatory workflow approval.
# EMAIL_DELIVERY_APPROVED — verified sender and delivery controls approval.
# LAUNCH_APPROVED — recorded release checklist approval; required in production.
